# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file, patches or ignores known vulnerabilities.
version: v1.25.1
# ignores vulnerabilities until expiry date; change duration by modifying expiry date
ignore:
  SNYK-JAVA-ORGJETBRAINSKOTLIN-2393744:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2020-29582: This vulnerability relates to information exposure via
          creation of temporary files (via Kotlin functions) with insecure
          permissions. Corda does not use any of the vulnerable functions so it
          not susceptible to this vulnerability.
        expires: 2029-08-01T01:00:00.000Z
        created: 2024-05-30T10:37:19.923Z
  SNYK-JAVA-ORGGRADLE-5750785:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2023-35947: This is a build-related vulnerability that does not
          affect the running of Corda. The Gradle build for Corda does not
          unpack any TAR archives. Corda is not exposed to this vulnerability.
        expires: 2029-08-01T01:00:00.000Z
        created: 2024-05-30T10:37:24.413Z
  SNYK-JAVA-JAKARTAVALIDATION-20936881:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-NOT-ASSIGNED: This is an improper input validation issue in
          Validation.byProvider(), where ProviderSpecificBootstrapImpl uses
          the single-argument AccessController.doPrivileged, allowing code
          running in a restricted ProtectionDomain to instantiate an arbitrary
          class's no-arg constructor with the library's permissions.
          Exploitation requires the JVM to run with a Java SecurityManager
          enabled, the library to be granted more permissions than the
          caller, and the attacker to already be able to run code in-process.
          Corda does not run with a Java SecurityManager, so no privilege
          elevation can occur. In addition, jakarta.validation-api is only
          pulled in transitively by Jersey (jersey-server), which Corda uses
          only in test tooling (node-driver), the demo webserver
          (testing/testserver) and sample applications, it is not part of the
          released Corda node. Hence Corda is not impacted by this
          vulnerability.
          This issue is only fixed in jakarta.validation-api@4.0.0-M1, a
          milestone release of Jakarta Validation 4.0, which is still under
          development and targets Jakarta EE 12. Corda 4.12 uses Jersey 3.1.x,
          which implements Jakarta EE 10 (Jakarta Validation 3.0), so the
          milestone API is not compatible with it and no fixed final release
          is available.
          Fix : jakarta.validation:jakarta.validation-api@4.0.0-M1
          Compatibility : Jakarta EE 12 (milestone), java 17+
        expires: 2029-08-01T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-11-06T00:00:00.000Z
patch: {}
